{"type": "thinking", "text": "Good, restored. Now the stats: ATK 89 STR 79 DEF 75.\n\nLet's compute: Attack 70 + prestige 9 = 79 + weapon 10 = 89. Strength 70 + weapon 9 = 79. Defense 70 + boots 5 = 75. Consistent. But what about Hitpoints? Maybe combat HP +150 infinite tower bonus. Where is HP shown? Maybe in fight screen only.\n\nNow maybe the \"stats list\" issue is about these values being calculated from fewer inputs — e.g., attack should include... hmm. Let me examine the Skills top tab maybe shows \"Combat stats\" with more detail. The Skills tab listed skills but no detailed bonuses.\n\nMaybe when you enter a dungeon, the fight screen shows a stats list (Attack, Strength, Defense, Hitpoints etc). Let's go into Dungeons and start a fight? The task says \"combat screen\" and preconditions \"No session is running\". Starting a fight would start a session — test might require it to see stats list. But \"the stats shown outside a fight\" — the stats list is outside a fight, i.e., on the combat screen (Dungeons/Gear/Skills). Hmm.\n\nActually wait. Let's reconsider: maybe the stats list is in the \"Skills\" top tab? No.\n\nCould be the Gear screen's stats line. \"ATK 89 STR 79 DEF 75\". The change: \"now calculated from fewer inputs.\" Before, it perhaps used total level + weapon + boots + prestige. Now perhaps omits something like prayer bonus or the infinite tower HP. Specifically, Attack: base 70 + weapon 10 + prestige 9 = 89 ✓. Strength: base 70 + weapon 9 = 79 ✓. Defense: 70 + boots 5 = 75 ✓. These match expected. So formula includes attack, weapon, prestige & boots. What other input would exist? Prayer gives no attack bonus in OSRS (prayer level doesn't add). Ranged/Magic irrelevant. So maybe no bug there.\n\nBut wait: \"Combat Lvl 80\". Let me compute the app's combat level formula. If the app defines combat level as max melee stats? 70+70+70+70 /4 = 70... Actually classic RS2 combat: \nbase = 0.25*(def + hp + floor(prayer/2)) = 0.25*(70+70+22)=40.5\nmelee = 0.325*(att+str) = 45.5 → 86\nSo combat level 86, not 80. Hmm, but prestige adds +9 attack and +4 hp; effective stats: attack 79, strength 70, defense 70, hitpoints 74, prayer 45 → base = 0.25*(70+74+22)=41.5; melee=0.325*(79+70)=48.425; total 89.9 → 89. Not 80.\n\nMaybe the app's combat level formula is simpler, e.g., average of combat skills? (70+70+70+70+40+40+45)/7 = 405/7 = 57.9. Not 80.\n\nMaybe combat level = max combat skill level + ...? Hmm.\n\nCould be total level 720: known skills. Let's sum: Attack 70, Strength 70, Defense 70, Hitpoints 70, Ranged 40, Magic 40, Prayer 45, Smithing 19, Mining 50, Mercantile 99 = 573. Remaining 147 across other skills (Woodcutting, Fishing, Cooking, Firemaking, Crafting, Fletching, Runecrafting, Herblore, Agility, Thieving, Slayer, Farming, Construction, Hunter, Summoning?) Unknown. So total level 720 plausible.\n\nCombat level \"80\" maybe = (att+str+def+hp)/4 + ... (280/4=70) + prayer? no. Hmm, maybe combat level = (att+str+def+hp+ranged+magic)/6? (70*4+40+40)/6=360/6=60. No.\n\nMaybe = max(att,str,def,hp,ranged,magic) + 10? 80. Hmm exactly 70+10? Could be level+prestige levels. Eh.\n\nNot worth reporting combat level without knowing formula. Focus on clear bugs.\n\nLet me explore the profile screen and pets tab now, then come back to combat.\n\nActually first, let me test \"Dungeons\" list: maybe entering a dungeon reveals stats list. Let's tap Dungeons then a low-level dungeon (Farm). That starts a session; but maybe first it shows a preparation screen with stats. Seems likely given \"stats shown outside a fight\".\n\nGo back to Dungeons."}
