ocal instead of hoisted, and it now resets on navigation/rotation. This is likely the deliberate bug! The other screens (combat) preserved scroll/tab selection? Let's check: On Combat, we selected Gear/Skills tabs and rotated would we see retention? Let's test after rotating back.\n\nActually, we should confirm the reset behavior thoroughly:\n- On the profile, select Pets, rotate → Skills (bug).\n- Also select Inventory, leave to Combat, return to Profile → Skills (bug?). Hmm, is leaving-and-returning expected to retain? Maybe not.\n\nAnother possibility: When rotating in landscape, the tab bar is cut off (Pets not visible) — can't navigate. But that's a different issue.\n\nLet me rotate back to portrait and verify state. Then repeat: select Pets → rotate to landscape → reset to Skills; rotate back → still Skills. That's consistent. Also maybe select Inventory then rotate: does it reset to Skills too? Probably.\n\nI think this is a reportable bug. But let's be careful about what the expected behavior is. Profile tab bar selection is UI state; rotating shouldn't reset it (standard Android behavior would restore). The preconditions and instructions say check rotate. So yes.\n\nAlso, the earlier observation: leaving Profile to Home and back reset the tab to Skills. Could be the same root cause (screen recreated on tab navigation). I could report one bug: selected profile tab is not retained when leaving/re-entering or rotating. The symptom: selected tab resets to Skills. Element: \"Skills\" tab. Observed quote: \"Skills\" (and GATHERING). Expected: Pets remains selected and pet list shown.\n\nBut before filing, ensure it's reproducible. Let me rotate back to portrait, confirm Skills, then tap Pets, rotate landscape again, confirm Skills.\n\nAlso note: after rotation, the Pets sidebar item wasn't visible; but content definitely Skills. This also indicates selected tab state lost.\n\nLet me rotate back."}
