ints to it. I'm fairly confident.\n\nWait, but there's another possibility: The bug is that the tab bar is *duplicated* between screens or the selection is tracked globally. Example: select Profile → Pets, then go to Combat → the combat screen might show Pets content? No, combat showed Dungeons after we were on Inventory? Hmm, when we switched from Profile (Inventory) to Combat, the combat screen showed Dungeons, fine.\n\nLet me also check: Profile tab selection resets upon leaving and coming back. That might be the same but without rotation. Let me verify with Pets: select Pets, go Home, back Profile → Skills. We already did exactly that earlier: selected Pets, tapped Home, came back → Skills. Yes.\n\nSo the selected tab is not persisted at all; it resets whenever the Profile screen is recreated (tab navigation away and back, or rotation). Is that \"bug\"? The feature change says selected tab now tracked by profile screen itself — perhaps tracking is only while the screen is alive. When you navigate away, the screen composable might be disposed. But a user would expect their selected tab to persist while in the profile and maybe across app navigation.\n\nHmm, the more robust bug: on rotation (configuration change), state should be preserved. Standard Android: rememberSaveable. A QA test would flag it. I'll report it.\n\nBefore that, let's finish testing other areas to find all bugs, then file reports.\n\nNow the pets tab change: \"pet list fetched together with the rest of the profile data.\" Possible bug: if profile data fetch fails or if pet list is empty until... But our list loaded fine. Maybe there's a subtle issue: the pet list initially renders \"NOT YET FOUND\" placeholder even though there are 30 pets? Wait, the \"NOT YET FOUND\" is probably the empty active-pet slot. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the bug: The Pets tab shows all 30 pets as owned-looking with colored icons while header says 0/30 obtained. Look at the screenshot of list scrolled: pets are fully colored. But at the top of the tab, \"NOT YET FOUND\" appears. Let me look at the top screenshot again by scrolling to top. Previously at first observation, the first pets' icons showed \"..\" (image placeholders) — need to see actual rendering. Let me scroll to top of Pets now after rotation reset. But wait, after rotate, Skills selected. Tap Pets; it will reset scroll to top. Let's do that and take a screenshot before scrolling."}
