{"type": "thinking", "text": "Very important observations:\n\n1. The pet icons/names are colored, not grayscale, even though \"0 / 30 obtained\" and \"NOT YET FOUND\" (the header says not yet found). But maybe \"NOT YET FOUND\" is the caption for the list section (i.e., not-yet-found pets list). Then showing them is expected.\n\n2. \"Tiny Templar\" has a fish icon and description \"A small fish...\" — clearly a data mismatch if the name is Tiny Templar. But maybe the pet is literally a tiny fish named Tiny Templar? Odd. Hmm — maybe the intended pet is \"Tiny Templar\" (prayer?) and its icon/description got mixed from another pet. Serious content bug? But it may be a pre-existing content issue, not the changed area. Still could report as a bug (wrong name/description/icon mismatch) if confident. Actually, wait: maybe the list is sorted and the Tiny Templar row is showing another pet's icon/description due to misalignment: the row order names: Dragon Whelp, Imp Pet, Baby Kraken, Rock Golem, Ent, Tiny Templar, Tangleroot. Icons: dragon, imp, kraken, rock golem, tree(Ent), fish, plant(Tangleroot). So only Tiny Templar is fish. If the fish pet should be e.g. \"Heron\", then name mismatch. Hmm. Possibly the game has a \"Tiny Templar\" pet that is a fish? Unlikely.\n\n3. Layout issue: The \"+10% XP\" bonus badge overlaps the description text for Ent: \"An ancient tree spirit that aids+10% XP your woodcutting.\" The badge is on the same line as description and it visually collides. Look: \"An ancient tree spirit that aids+10% XP\" — there's no space; the badge overlaps the word \"aids\"? Actually screenshot shows \"An ancient tree spirit that aids+10% XP\" on one line, with \"+10% XP\" appended immediately, and \"your woodcutting.\" below. Similarly Tiny Templar: \"A small fish that boosts your +10% XP fishing expertise.\" The badge overlaps into the text area. For Dragon Whelp: \"A young dragon that boosts +5% XP your combat prowess.\" The badge is right-aligned at the end