rs dimmed (names/descriptions are grayish). Hmm, the whole pets area looks dimmed/faded compared to other tabs — the names are grey not white. Maybe that's the \"not yet found\" styling (dimmed). The icons are colored but could be intentional.\n\nLet me compare an owned pet appearance. We have no owned pets (0/30). So can't compare.\n\n5. Count \"0 / 30 obtained\" and \"0%\" consistent. The progress bar is nearly empty but shows a small blue line. Fine.\n\nNow, the pet list \"fetched together with the rest of the profile data\" — did it actually fetch 30 pets? Yes. Maybe the bug is that the pet list is only fetched once and doesn't update? Hmm.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug is: pets that are NOT obtained should not show their details (or should show locked), but the app shows them fully. But that's likely by design (a collection grid).\n\nLet me look for a more concrete bug: In the pet list, \"Tiny Templar\" is a fish — clear data inconsistency. Let me check if the same pet appears elsewhere (e.g., Bestiary? no). There's no other source.\n\nHmm, maybe this is actually a hint about the pets list being fetched incorrectly: the pet *names* come from one index and *descriptions/icons* from another, off by one! Let's check whether names align with descriptions after the Tiny Templar row:\n- Tangleroot (plant icon, farming description) ✓\n- Gothic Emberling (magic description) ✓\n- Void Wisp (combat) ✓\n- Graceling Sprite (agility) ✓\n- Shadow Fox (thieving) ✓\n- Ember Moth (?), +10% XP\n- Herb Wisp (herblore) ✓\n- Rune Sprite (runecrafting) ✓\n- Gem Golem (crafting?) ✓\n- Feather Drake (fletching) ✓\n- Forge Imp (smithing) ✓\n- Coin Drake (coins?) +10% XP\n- Timber Sprite (construction?) +10% XP\n- Juggling Imp (all skills) ✓\n- Stone Guardian (combat) ✓\n- Solstice Sprite (combat) ✓\n- Lantern Wisp (combat) ✓\n- Grave Sprout (farming?) +5% XP\n- Golden Goose (coins) ✓\n- Sunbird Chick (?), +5% XP\n- Frost Wyrmling (?), +5%\n- Snowhare (fishing) ✓ (+5% XP)\n- Petal Sprite (combat) ✓\n- Bumblebee (herblore) ✓\n\nOnly Tiny Templar mismatched. So not shifted.\n\nMaybe the pet name \"Tiny Templar\" is a fish (a \"templar\" fish?). A \"Tiny Templar\" could be a small temple guardian... description \"A small fish\" doesn't fit. But content bugs in seed data are hard to verify. I'd rather not report unless the change hints at it.\n\nWait — \"Pets tab: the pet list is now fetched together with the rest of the profile data.\" Maybe the bug: pet list is loaded from profile data, which may be capped or includes wrong owner. Since 0 pets owned, maybe there's nothing to verify. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the other profile tabs for comparison, especially \"Bonuses\" which may show pet bonuses. And \"Achievements\" (0%). Maybe there's inconsistency: the pets tab shows 30 pets and 0/30, but Achievements might show something.\n\nI think the two likely seeded bugs:\nA. Profile selected tab resets on rotation/navigation (state not tracked/preserved).\nB. Combat stats list missing an input (e.g., the \"ATK\" doesn't include prestige +9? But it does: 89 = 70+10+9).\n\nHmm wait, let me re-examine: Is the ATK 89 correct? Base Attack level 70, prestige bonus +9, Iron Sword Atk +10 → 89. Yes. STR 79 = 70+9. DEF 75 = 70+5. But wait, what about the Bronze Boots Def +5 — yes.\n\nBut what about \"Attack owns Precision tiers I and II\" — maybe Precision adds attack bonus too? Preconditions: \"Prestige: Attack and Hitpoints are each prestiged once, Attack owns Precision tiers I and II and Hitpoints owns Vitality tier I (combat stat prestige bonuses +9 Attack and +4 Hitpoints).\" So +9 includes Precision tiers. OK.\n\nSo stats are consistent.\n\nWhat \"fewer inputs\" could mean: The stats list outside a fight might have previously included e.g. the equipped weapon and boots; now maybe it's missing the weapon in some circumstances. We saw it included when Attack style selected. Let me verify the stats list updates when we unequip the sword, or equip a different weapon. Test reversal: Unequip Iron Sword → ATK should drop from 89 to 79 and STR 79→70. Then re-equip. This tests whether the stats list uses live equipment (input). The change \"calculated from fewer inputs\" might mean it no longer recalculates when equipment changes. Let's test!\n\nGo Combat > Gear tab (top tabs), Attack", "truncated": true}
