{"type": "thinking", "text": "Good.\n\nNow \"stats shown outside a fight are now calculated from fewer inputs\" — maybe the issue is that the stats list omits the *Infinite Tower* +150 HP and prestige bonuses? But no HP in that list. Or maybe the stats list in the skills tab? Hmm.\n\nLet me look for another stats list: In the Gear tab, ATK/STR/DEF. That's it. In the dungeon sheet, recommended vs your combat level. In fight, stats.\n\n\"Combat screen stats list: the stats shown outside a fight are now calculated from fewer inputs.\" Could refer to this \"ATK 89 STR 79 DEF 75\" being computed with only base stats + equipment, but ignoring prestige? It shows 89 so no.\n\nWait — maybe it's this: the stat list previously showed more combat stats (e.g., \"ATK, STR, DEF, HP\" or \"Ranged/Magic\") but now only 3. If the change intentionally simplified to \"fewer inputs\", the seeded bug could be that it now ignores the weapon when the style is Ranged/Magic — i.e., the values don't change when equipping a ranged weapon. But no ranged weapon in inventory.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the \"stats list\" is the Skills tab list which shows combat skills levels and XP; \"calculated from fewer inputs\" might mean it calculates XP from level incorrectly. Hmm.\n\nHmm, maybe I should look at the \"Skills\" profile screen or combat Skills tab numbers vs the Known preconditions for a mismatch. Precondition: \"Smithing level 19 with 4,400 XP\". In profile Skills grid, Smithing shows level 19 (no XP). In the combat Skills tab there's no Smithing. Maybe the Smithing card, when tapped, shows XP. Let me check: Profile > Skills > Smithing shows level 19; detailed XP 4,400 expected somewhere. Not in scope though.\n\nGiven the combat stats list shows correctly and live, maybe no bug there. But the task said \"sweep these areas\", not necessarily each changed item has a bug. There may be bugs in profile nav (rotation reset) and pets (maybe description mismatch).\n\nLet me investigate the pets tab more: maybe the pet list is sorted incorrectly? The \"NOT YET FOUND\" section lists 30 pets; no owned. Another bug: the top progress \"0 / 30 obtained\" says there are 30 pets, and the list indeed has 30. Good.\n\nCould there be a bug that pet list is not loaded when first opening Pets directly after app start? We did: app start → home → profile → Skills default → Pets; loaded fine. Could test from cold: not possible (app already open; can force-stop? open_app doesn't reset data but maybe brings foreground; we can't force-stop without adb).\n\nMaybe the pet list bug is that after rotation, while Pets tab resets to Skills, re-selecting Pets reloads the pet list — fine.\n\nHmm, maybe the \"profile tab bar selected tab tracked by profile screen itself\" bug is something else: The *combat* screen's top tab bar (Dungeons/Gear/Skills) might use the same state as the profile tab bar! E.g., selecting \"Gear\" in profile switches combat top tab to Gear. Let's test: On profile, select \"Gear\" (profile sidebar). Then go to Combat screen. Combat top tabs default to Dungeons normally. If it shows Gear, then state is shared/leaked. That'd be a clear \"tab tracked by profile screen itself\" bug (selection leaking). Actually the change says selected tab tracked by the profile screen itself (not shared), so a bug might be exactly cross-screen leakage: e.g., selecting Pets then going Combat shows... We went Profile(Pets) → Combat earlier and Combat showed Dungeons. So no leak.\n\nWhat about the bottom nav \"Profile\" indicator? Fine.\n\nLet me test the tab selection more precisely with a fresh sequence: On Profile, tap \"Bonuses\", then tap \"Achievements\", check content and highlight each time. Maybe the highlight doesn't update (stuck on previous) or the content lags one behind. The change \"selected tab is now tracked by the profile screen itself\" could introduce an off-by-one or stale selection: e.g., tapping Pets shows Banners content with Pets highlighted. We saw Pets → pets content and highlight, so that works at least for Pets. Test a few more.\n\nLet me tap Bonuses (18) and observe."}
