{"type": "thinking", "text": "Back portrait at Skills. Good.\n\nNow let me file the profile tab state bug. But first let me confirm the exact behavior once more with minimal steps maybe the report should describe: \"Open Profile, select Inventory/Pets, rotate device → selection resets to Skills and Skills content shows.\" We reproduced twice (Pets and Inventory). Good.\n\nObservation quote: \"GATHERING\" (Skills content shown after rotation) and \"Skills\" highlighted. Expected: Pets/Inventory content retained. Use element_ref from latest observe: element 10 is \"Skills\" sidebar. Hmm, the element showing the defect: the Skills tab highlighted while expected Pets. But current observe after rotating back shows Skills content; the bug is the reset. I'd point to element_ref 10 (\"Skills\" tab selected) or 20 (\"GATHERING\"). The report requires quoting exact on-screen text that shows the defect: \"GATHERING\" or \"0 / 30 obtained\" absent. I'd quote \"GATHERING\" since that's the Skills content replacing Pets.\n\nBut wait — before filing, let me finish testing pets and combat fully. Also consider coins display 2.5M. Let me evaluate that: 2,567,890. Formatted as \"2.5M\" — many idle games show one decimal truncated. If the app rounds, should be 2.6M. Could be a seeded bug? The precondition explicitly gives exact coins 2,567,890 and the display 2.5M. In many QA scenarios, the expected display would be \"2.57M\" or \"2.6M\"; \"2.5M\" could be a truncation bug. But without knowing format, risky. However, the tests say \"Consistency: check that what each screen shows agrees with the data\". The home and profile both show 2.5M consistently. Maybe the intended display is 2.6M. Hmm.\n\nLet's check other values to infer formatting: Total Level 720 exact. Combat 80 exact. Coins 2.5M. If the format uses one decimal and rounds, 2.6M. If it floors/truncates, 2.5M. Which is likely? Common implementation: `String.format(\"%.1fM\", coins/1_000_000.0)` → 2.6M. Truncation via integer division → 2.5M. Can't know. There might be another screen showing exact coins (Shop) where I could verify exact balance 2,567,890. But doesn't resolve display rule.\n\nMaybe the coin value is 2,567,890 and \"2.5M\" is intentionally the expected display (floor). The preconditions give exact value for consistency checks with calculations (e.g., shop prices, rewards). I'd lean not a bug.\n\nWhat about the \"Combat Level 80\"? Let me compute using the game's likely formula. Perhaps the game's combat level = average of (Attack, Strength, Defense, Hitpoints) + 10 = 70+10 = 80? Or max combat level + prestige levels? Hmm. In many idle games, \"Combat Level\" = sum of combat skill levels / 4 = 70. Not 80. Maybe (Att+Str+Def+HP)/4 + (Ranged+Magic+Prayer)/... \n\nLet's derive: 70,70,70,70,40,40,45 → 80. Possible formula: melee based: 0.25*(def+hp+floor(prayer/2)) = 40.5, plus 0.325*(att+str)=45.5 → 86. With prestige +9 attack & +4 hp, ~90. Not 80.\n\nMaybe they use: combat level = max of (attack+strength)/2, (ranged*1.5?), ... e.g., (att+str)/2 = 70; + something? Hmm.\n\nCould be the app shows an intentionally simplified \"combat level\" = (Attack + Strength + Defense + Hitpoints)/4 + 10? = 80. If the character is strong (70s), +10. Weird.\n\nOr maybe combat level 80 comes from level 70 + 10 (max level cap?) Eh. Not enough info; don't report.\n\nLet me check the Quests screen \"3 guild quests\" not in scope. Skip.\n\nLet me now systematically test the Pets tab for state issues:\n- Select Pets, scroll down, switch to another profile tab, return to Pets: does the scroll position reset? (probably fine)\n- Select Pets, rotate: reset to Skills (bug already).\n- Pet count consistency: 0/30 and 30 list entries. Good.\n- With 0 pets, \"NOT YET FOUND\" is the section header. Perhaps the bug: \"NOT YET FOUND\" should only appear if pets are not found, and it does.\n- Pet bonus values: some show \"+10% XP\", some \"+5% XP\", \"+3% XP\", \"+10% Coins\". Do these have any inconsistency with descriptions? \"Coin Drake\" says \"uncanny nose for profit\" but gives +10% XP, not coins. Hmm! That's a mismatch: Coin Drake description is about coins/profit, but its bonus is \"+10% XP\". Also \"Golden Goose\" description about coins gives +10% Coins, consistent. \"Coin Drake\" probably should give +10% Coins. Is that a bug? It's a content/logic inconsistency. But maybe Coin Drake boosts XP? The description says \"a dragon hatchling raised on a diet of gold coins. It has an uncanny nose for profit.\" → should be +10% Coins. Yet shows +10% XP. Hmm, possible seeded bug in pet data? But the change is about fetching the pet list, not pet definitions. Data could still be seeded anywhere.\n\nSimilarly \"Timber Sprite\" description about construction → +10% XP? could be construction XP, fine. \"Ember Moth\" no skill mentioned +10% XP. \"Gem Golem\" +10% XP (crafting). \"Sunbird Chick\", \"Frost Wyrmling\", \"Petal Sprite\", \"Grave Sprout\", \"Bumblebee\" +5% XP. Those descriptions mention battle/potions etc. Hard to verify.\n\nBut \"Coin Drake\" +10% XP vs Golden Goose +10% Coins is suspicious. However, maybe Coin Drake boosts coins... no, label clearly +10% XP. Hmm. Also many pets \"boost skill XP\" so +10% XP is generic. The pet named \"Coin Drake\" giving XP is odd but could be \"combat XP\"? No.\n\nAlso \"Tiny Templar\" fish. These are likely deliberate content bugs in the seed? The changed area is \"Pets tab: the pet list is now fetched together with the rest of the profile data.\" Perhaps the bug is that pet bonuses aren't fetched correctly from profile data, showing defaults (+5%/+10% XP) for all pets instead of actual bonuses. Hmm! Look: pets' bonuses seem simplified: most show +5% or +10% XP, with a few +3% XP, +10% Coins. Maybe the correct bonuses should vary by skill but the display only shows \"+X% XP\" without skill name, so it's fine.\n\nWait, maybe the \"pet list fetched with rest of profile data\" bug is that the pet list appears even when not obtained (all 30). But \"NOT YET FOUND\" section implies deliberate collection display.\n\nI should check other screens that reference pets. Maybe the \"Bonuses\" tab should list pet bonuses for owned pets only; 0 owned so none.\n\nHmm. Maybe I should test the Pets tab's scrolling to the very bottom: it showed Bumblebee as last, then maybe a final element \"Pet bonuses apply...\"? We reached bottom at Bumblebee, seems complete (30). Fine.\n\nIs there a search/filter for pets? No.\n\nLet me count the pets observed: \n1 Dragon Whelp\n2 Imp Pet\n3 Baby Kraken\n4 Rock Golem\n5 Ent\n6 Tiny Templar\n7 Tangleroot\n8 Gothic Emberling\n9 Void Wisp\n10 Graceling Sprite\n11 Shadow Fox\n12 Ember Moth\n13 Herb Wisp\n14 Rune Sprite\n15 Gem Golem\n16 Feather Drake\n17 Forge Imp\n18 Coin Drake\n19 Timber Sprite\n20 Juggling Imp\n21 Stone Guardian\n22 Solstice Sprite\n23 Lantern Wisp\n24 Grave Sprout\n25 Golden Goose\n26 Sunbird Chick\n27 Frost Wyrmling\n28 Snowhare\n29 Petal Sprite\n30 Bumblebee\n= 30 ✓.\n\nSo the list is complete.\n\nNow, \"pet list is now fetched together with the rest of the profile data\" — maybe the intended bug: if you obtain a pet (can't), list updates. Not testable.\n\nLet me now test the profile \"Gear\" tab (sidebar) which might be a stats list too. It might show equipment + combat stats. Let's inspect. Tap Gear (12)."}
