{"type": "thinking", "text": "Again resets to Skills after leaving. Is this behavior expected? The change was specifically \"the selected tab is now tracked by the profile screen itself.\" If the profile screen is recreated when re-entering, it resets. A user might expect last tab retained, but many apps reset to default. Hmm.\n\nThe stronger defect is rotation: Android expects state retention across configuration changes. The QA instructions explicitly call rotation. I'll report that.\n\nBut wait — maybe there's a bigger bug: The selected tab isn't just reset; the *sidebar highlight* and *content* mismatch? After rotation, both Skills highlighted and Skills content, so consistent, just reset.\n\nLet's test if other tabs also reset: Inventory → rotate → Skills (done, consistent).\n\nI'll file one report for the profile tab state loss on rotation/re-entry. Steps: Open Profile > select Pets (+ content) > rotate to landscape > content/selection resets to Skills. Expected: Pets remains selected. Observed quote \"GATHERING\" or \"0 / 30 obtained\". Element ref: current observe element 13 is Pets? No, after rotating back we're on Skills. I need to capture the state right after rotation to get an element ref and quote. I already have the landscape observe from Inventory rotation: element 9 \"Skills\", element 13 \"GATHERING\". I can report using that latest landscape observation? The latest observe is portrait. The report field element_ref should be from latest observe. Hmm, \"the number of the element showing the defect, from your latest observe (the element itself, or the closest one when something is missing)\". Latest observe: element 10 \"Skills\" (selected tab) or 20 \"GATHERING\". I can quote \"GATHERING\" which is on screen now. But the defect (reset) isn't currently visible as a defect without context. I think it's acceptable: element 10 Skills tab, quote \"GATHERING\" showing Skills content instead of Pets. Hmm, the quote must show the defect. Maybe better to rep