{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed. Now file the report while on this screen. element_ref 13 = \"GATHERING\" (Skills content). The selected tab \"Skills\" element 9. The defect is the Pets selection lost. Symptom type: not_persisted. Screen \"Profile (Pets tab)\". Element \"Profile tab bar / Pets tab selection\". Field \"selected tab\". Expected \"Pets tab stays selected and pet list shows\". Observed \"GATHERING\" and Skills selected. Steps.\n\nWait, but is this really a bug? Let me consider more. The change \"selected tab is now tracked by the profile screen itself\" — maybe they intentionally made it so the profile screen maintains its own selected tab state, which resets when recreated. The QA expected behavior from the change likely is: when you switch bottom tabs, the profile's selected sub-tab persists? Hmm. In many apps, the bottom navigation keeps screens alive; profile screen's state would persist across bottom tab switches. Here it resets, suggesting the state isn't actually retained (maybe because selected tab is tracked in a remember (not rememberSaveable) or because the screen recomposes). The regression likely: \"selected tab resets when navigating away and back\" — a state persistence bug. That's a valid finding.\n\nHowever, I want to be careful not to file a false report that gets rejected. The developer will reply; if they say by design, fine but confirmed reports are logged. The instruction says a quote that was never on screen gets rejected. Our quote is valid on screen.\n\nLet me file it.\n\nActually, hold on. Before filing, let's think about whether \"selected tab tracked by the profile screen itself\" could mean the opposite bug: the profile tab selection should reset when entering the profile (fresh), and previously it persisted (global), and now it doesn't. That's the intended change. In that case, the reset on re-entry is intended, BUT reset on rotation? \"tracked by the profile screen itself\" — when the activity rotates, the screen is recreated, so state going to default may be acceptable but typically not (Android saves state). The QA guidelines explicitly mention rotation as a check, so likely seeded.\n\nHmm, but if the selected tab is tracked by the profile screen itself, and the screen is recreated on rotation, losing it is arguably expected unless rememberSaveable used. Device rotation is a standard test. I'd report it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the \"profile tab bar\" refers to the *bottom* nav tab bar? No, \"Profile tab bar\" likely the sub-tabs. Hmm. \"the selected tab is now tracked by the profile screen itself\" — the change is about the sub-tab selection state ownership. A classic bug: the sub-tab selection isn't reset when you navigate away, so when you come back you see a different tab than default; or it doesn't reflect correctly. But we see reset, so maybe that's correct default behavior.\n\nWait, maybe I should test whether the selected tab *stays* when navigating within profile and back to profile... The change might be about the \"tab bar\" being shared across screens: e.g., the selected sub-tab is now tracked by the profile screen, so when you tap \"Gear\" in profile and then go to Combat > Gear, then back to Profile, previously it might show Gear (retained globally), now resets to Skills. The bug could be that the sub-tab selection is lost when navigating away, which is intentionally the new behavior? The changelog just states the implementation, not the desired UX.\n\nLet's look for other candidate bugs before deciding. We have time.\n\nCombat screen: The stats list outside a fight is calculated from fewer inputs. Let me test the stats with equipment from inventory, e.g., equipping best gear in combat. But we verified.\n\nWhat about the stats list for Ranged/Magic styles: selecting Ranged shows \"ATK 79 STR 70 DEF 75\" — but the actual combat style is Ranged, whose hit chance should use Ranged level 40, not Attack 79. The stats list doesn't show Ranged at all. Is that a bug? The label \"ATK\" is misleading when Ranged selected. Hmm, but maybe the game's stats list always shows melee stats + defense. That seems like a design flaw.\n\nWait, look at the dungeon sheet: \"Combat Style: Attack\". Selecting Ranged loadout may show \"Combat Style: Ranged\". The stats list on Gear for Ranged shows ATK 79 STR 70 DEF 75. Since the character has Ranged 40, the attack bonus with no ranged weapon... The list should probably show RNG 40? There's no \"RNG\" label anywhere. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the \"fewer inputs\" bug is precisely that the stats list used to show Attack/Strength/Defense **plus** the selected style's relevant skill, and now it dropped Ranged/Magic. But no baseline.\n\nLet me examine the \"Gear\" list under Ranged: it shows a \"Weapon (Ranged)\" slot, \"Arrow\" spinner. If you equip nothing, stats line should perhaps be \"ATK 79 STR 70 DEF 75\" reflecting melee equipment bonuses. For Ranged with no weapon, the damage would be based on Ranged level 40. The stat line doesn't show it, so a Ranged player sees wrong/misleading stats. But if Ranged is untrained/unsupported beyond level 40, maybe.\n\nHmm, the app likely calculates combat stats as: attack = attack level + weapon attack bonus; strength = strength level + weapon strength bonus; defense = defense level + armour defense. For ranged style, the \"attack\" would be ranged level + weapon ranged bonus? The code change \"calculated from fewer inputs\" might have replaced a full computation with a simpler one that only considers melee. The bug could be that selecting Ranged/Magic doesn't change the stats list.\n\nLet me test with an equipped Ranged weapon — none in inventory (no bow). So can't test.\n\nMaybe Magic: \"Spell\" spinner empty; no spell available. So Ranged/Magic unusable. Fine.\n\nLet's re-read the changelog line: \"Combat screen stats list: the stats shown outside a fight are now calculated from fewer inputs.\" This sounds like a refactor that could cause missing bonuses. We verified base+weapon+boots+prestige. What other input could the stats list have used? Perhaps the **Prayer** level (45) to add a hidden attack/strength/defense boost? In this game, prayer might boost combat stats. The Bonuses tab would show it. Let me check profile Bonuses: no Prayer row. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the \"fewer inputs\" removed the **Infinite Tower +150 HP** from the HP stat on the combat screen outside a fight? But HP isn't shown outside a fight (only in fight). Actually, the combat screen **Skills** tab shows Hitpoints level 70 and XP, not HP 890. The fight shows HP 890/890. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe \"stats list\" refers to the fight screen's stats display, and \"outside a fight\" means the dungeon detail sheet's \"Your combat level 80\" vs recommended. Hmm.\n\nActually, re-reading: \"Combat screen stats list: the stats shown outside a fight are now calculated from fewer inputs.\" Could mean the list of combat stats on the Combat screen (the stats panel) that is visible when no fight is running. On the Gear tab, the list \"ATK 89 STR 79 DEF 75\" is exactly \"stats shown outside a fight\". So yes. The change says \"calculated from fewer inputs.\" A bug would be e.g. the stats list forgot to include the **equipped weapon's** bonus — but we tested and it includes. Or forgot the **prestige** bonus — includes. Or forgot the **boots** — includes. Or forgot **base level** — includes. It even updates live. So no bug in those.\n\nHmm, unless the bug is with **armour** other than boots: we could equip a body armour (Runite Platebody) which likely gives Def bonus; check DEF updates. Inventory has many platebodies. Equipping one might be a bigger data change but reversible. Let's test: go to Combat Gear, Body None, pick Runite Platebody; see if DEF increases. Actually expected bonuses depend on item. Let's see the item's Def value in picker. This tests whether the stats list includes body armour. If it only includes weapon and boots (fewer inputs!), maybe body armour is ignored → bug. Ooh, \"calculated from fewer inputs\" might be exactly that: it only sums weapon + boots, ignoring body/legs/head/shield. Let's test with body armour and helmet.\n\nWe have Mithril Platebody, Adamantite Platebody, Slayer Platebody, Runite Chainbody, Runite Platebody, Gilded Platebody, Steel Full Helmet, Mithril Med Helm", "truncated": true}
