xactly what we see. The changelog itself doesn't call it a bug, but it introduced a regression: selection no longer survives.\n\nI think this is the intended bug. Let me file it.\n\nBut before filing, I want to test the pets tab state on rotation too: The pet list resets scroll position when re-selecting Pets (probably) — minor.\n\nAlso, let me test the pets tab count/bonuses maybe via the \"Armory\" or \"Achievements\" screen. Hmm.\n\nAnother angle: The changed pets fetch may have introduced a bug where the Pets tab shows the list only after the profile data loads; if you tap Pets immediately after app launch, maybe it shows empty/\"NOT YET FOUND\" list incorrectly. We can't reproduce cold start easily, but we can maybe force-stop via Settings > Apps? That's heavy and changes state. Not needed.\n\nLet me look at the \"Achievements\" tab and \"Notes\" etc. to ensure navigation works (nothing broken). Quick taps.\n\nActually, the profile tab bar bug may also manifest as: after selecting a tab, the *highlight* doesn't update until the content reloads? No.\n\nLet me test rapid tab switching to see if selection/content desync: tap Inventory, Pets, Bonuses, Achievements quickly, then observe. The content should match the last tap. This tests \"repetition\" and state. Let me do with waits? We can tap sequentially in one call each.\n\nActually file the rotation bug now. Then continue.\n\nLet me compose the report:\n\nscreen: \"Profile (Pets tab)\"\nelement: \"Profile section tab bar / selected tab\"\nfield: \"Selected tab\"\nsymptom_type: \"not_persisted\"\nexpected: \"After rotating the device, the Pets tab stays selected and the pet list remains visible.\"\nobserved: \"After rotating, the tab resets to Skills and the Skills content (GATHERING) is shown instead of the pet list.\"\nsteps: [\"Open the Profile tab\", \"Tap Pets in the profile tab bar\", \"Confirm the Pets list is shown (0 / 30 obtained)\", \"Rotate the device to landscape\", \"Observe the profile tab bar shows Skills selected and GATHERING content\"]\nelement_ref: 13 (GATHERING) or 9 (Skills). The \"element itself\" showing the defect is the Skills tab highlight or the content. I'll use 13 (GATHERING) since quote is GATHERING. Hmm, expected missing quote? observed_quote \"GATHERING\" exact on screen. Good.\n\nWait, the latest observe is portrait now (after revert). element_ref 13 corresponds to \"Body\" not GATHERING. The rule: \"number of the element showing the defect, from your latest observe\". Latest observe: [13] \"Body\" None. That would be wrong. I need to be on the defective state at the time of filing, or use the latest observe elements. Let me re-trigger: tap Pets, rotate landscape, observe (elements 9 Skills, 13 GATHERING), then file. Then rotate back.\n\nDo it."}
