{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now continue investigating pets and combat for other bugs.\n\nPotential pet bug candidates:\n1. Tiny Templar being a fish with fishing description — likely a data bug (name vs. icon/description). Is it \"wrong value\"? The pet's name is \"Tiny Templar\" but the icon is a fish and the description \"A small fish that boosts your fishing expertise.\" It should probably be a fish pet name (e.g., \"Heron\"?) or a templar. This is a real inconsistency on screen. Could report as \"wrong_value\" with element_ref 45 (Tiny Templar) and quote \"A small fish that boosts your fishing expertise.\" Hmm, but what's expected? The name \"Tiny Templar\" doesn't match. Could this be intentional? \"Tiny Templar\" could be a tiny fish templar? No.\n\nLet me search memory: Idle Fantasy is a real app? Pets list: Dragon Whelp, Imp Pet, Baby Kraken, Rock Golem, Ent, Tiny Templar, Tangleroot... OSRS pets: Baby mole, Beaver, Heron, Rock golem, Tangleroot, etc. \"Tiny Templar\" might be a pet from a different game. In this app, maybe the fishing pet is \"Tiny Templar\" — weird. Actually the description \"A small fish that boosts your fishing expertise\" strongly implies the pet is a fish. The icon is a fish. The name Tiny Templar could be a joke (a tiny fish wearing a templar helmet?) but the icon is just a blue fish. Hmm.\n\nI'd be cautious. The pet list is a changed area, so the seeded bug might be exactly a mismatched pet entry (name vs description). The changelog says \"the pet list is now fetched together with the rest of the profile data\" — a fetch refactor could cause misalignment of pet metadata (name from one source, description from another). A single mismatch (Tiny Templar) could be a data error though.\n\nWait, maybe all pet descriptions are one index off from names? Let's map the first 7:\n- Dragon Whelp (dragon icon) → \"A young dragon that boosts your combat prowess.\" ✓\n- Imp Pet (imp icon) → \"A mischievous imp that enhances your prayer training.\" ✓\n- Baby Kraken (kraken icon) → \"A tiny kraken that improves your cooking abilities.\" ✓\n- Rock Golem (rock icon) → \"A living rock formation that enhances your mining prowess.\" ✓\n- Ent (tree icon) → \"An ancient tree spirit that aids your woodcutting.\" ✓\n- Tiny Templar (fish icon) → \"A small fish that boosts your fishing expertise.\" ✗ name\n- Tangleroot (plant icon) → \"A magical plant creature that enhances your farming.\" ✓\n\nSo only the name is off. Maybe the actual pet name for fishing is \"Tiny Templar\"? Could the game have a \"Tiny Templar\" fish? Hmm. Let me see other pet names: \"Graceling Sprite\" for agility, \"Shadow Fox\" thieving, \"Herb Wisp\" herblore, \"Rune Sprite\" runecrafting, \"Gem Golem\" crafting, \"Feather Drake\" fletching, \"Forge Imp\" smithing, \"Coin Drake\", \"Timber Sprite\", \"Juggling Imp\", \"Stone Guardian\", \"Solstice Sprite\", \"Lantern Wisp\", \"Grave Sprout\", \"Golden Goose\", \"Sunbird Chick\", \"Frost Wyrmling\", \"Snowhare\", \"Petal Sprite\", \"Bumblebee\". The fishing pet could be \"Tiny Templar\"?? No. Maybe the fishing pet is a \"fish\" called \"Tiny Templar\" as a pun? Unlikely.\n\nActually wait — maybe the community/OSRS \"Tiny Tempor\" (a fish-like pet from Tempoross, the fishing boss)! Yes! OSRS has a pet called \"Tiny Tempor\" — a tiny fish from the Tempoross boss, obtained from fishing. The name in this app is \"Tiny Templar\" — close to \"Tiny Tempor\" but wrong. Hmm, \"Tiny Templar\" vs \"Tiny Tempor\" — one letter? Templar = T-e-m-p-l-a-r; Tempor = T-e-m-p-o-r. The app's name \"Tiny Templar\" may be its own rename to avoid IP. And it's a fish (Tiny Tempor is a fish). So \"Tiny Templar\" being a small fish is plausible/intentional! OK, not a bug.\n\n2. \"Coin Drake\" giving +10% XP instead of +10% Coins. Given Golden Goose gives +10% Coins, Coin Drake should likely give coins. But maybe its bonus is \"combat XP\"? Description says nose for profit. Hmm. Could be intentional? Let me look at the bonuses on the Bonuses tab for pets — but 0 obtained so not listed. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the pet list bug is that the bonuses shown are wrong (all XP). But no way to verify without pet definitions.\n\n3. Count \"0 / 30 obtained\" but header \"NOT YET FOUND\" and colored list. Hmm.\n\nLet me instead test the pets tab consistency with the \"Profile\" header data: 0 pets obtained, and the \"Bonuses\" tab has no pet entries. Consistent.\n\nMaybe there's a hidden bug: the pet list shows \"+10% XP\" bonus for pets, but the Bonuses tab only lists bonuses the player has. Since no pets, none. Fine.\n\nWhat about the \"Pets\" tab when profile data refresh fails? Not testable.\n\nLet's check the Achievements tab and Banners/Notes/Bestiary/Armory quickly to see if navigation loads content (part of profile/navigation). Maybe one tab is broken (blank) — that could be a bug. Tap Achievements (14)."}
