ity placeholder for image content. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug: \"NOT YET FOUND\" header is displayed even though the section below has all pets; maybe it should say \"NOT YET FOUND (30)\" or hide bonuses. Not verifiable.\n\nLet me check the **pet list's bonus numbers vs the pet's description skill**: e.g., the pet \"Imp Pet\" description \"enhances your prayer training\" and bonus \"+5% XP\" (generic). Should maybe say \"+5% Prayer XP\". But the Armory shows item stats; the pets display \"+10% XP\" without skill. Could be by design. However, if the pet bonus is wrong (e.g., a mining pet should give +10% Mining XP but shows just +10% XP), that's incomplete but ambiguous.\n\nMaybe there's a bug where **all pets show the same \"+5% XP\"/\"+10% XP\"** because the fetch uses a default, not the real bonus. Since pets are all unowned, maybe the UI should show the bonus per pet; it does vary (5/10/3, coins). Could still be wrong values (e.g., Tiny Templar should give +10% Fishing XP, shows +10% XP generic). Hmm.\n\nLet me inspect the **Infinite Tower** and other content? Out of scope.\n\nAlternatively, for #2, maybe the bug is that the **Pets tab shows a \"0 / 30 obtained\" count but the list is missing the 30th pet** due to an off-by-one. We counted 30. Did we really see 30 distinct? Yes.\n\nWait, the header count \"0 / 30\" and the list has 30. But are there exactly 30? Let me recount from observations: 7 (Dragon Whelp, Imp Pet, Baby Kraken, Rock Golem, Ent, Tiny Templar, Tangleroot) + 5 (Gothic Emberling, Void Wisp, Graceling Sprite, Shadow Fox, Ember Moth) + 5 (Herb Wisp, Rune Sprite, Gem Golem, Feather Drake, Forge Imp) + 5 (Coin Drake, Timber Sprite, Juggling Imp, Stone Guardian, Solstice Sprite) + 4 (Lantern Wisp, Grave Sprout, Golden Goose, Sunbird Chick) + 4 (Frost Wyrmling, Snowhare, Petal Sprite, Bumblebee) = 30. Yes.\n\nHmm, maybe the **pet list order** has \"Tiny Templar\" in the wrong place alphabetically? Pets aren't sorted A-Z. No sort control. So no.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the pet list is fetched with profile data but **the Pets tab doesn't refresh when the profile data updates** (e.g., after leveling, the Pets list should show newly unlocked pets). Can't test.\n\nLet me look at the \"Pets\" tab in the **Bonuses** context: maybe pet bonuses are also listed in the Bonuses tab with source \"Pets\"; but 0 pets so none.\n\nI might not find a pets bug. But the changelog says \"the pet list is now fetched together with the rest of the profile data.\" Maybe this change is benign and included just to distract, or its bug is subtle (e.g., the pet list fetch causes a crash on some data). Hmm.\n\nFor #3, similarly benign? The stats list was verifiably correct. But maybe I haven't tested the right thing. Let me look for another \"stats list\" on the Combat screen: the **Dungeons tab** list of dungeons is a list, not stats. The **Gear tab** has the ATK/STR/DEF list. The **Skills tab** has the skill list. The **Combat Log tab** (during session) has the stats list (HP + ATK/STR/DEF). Hmm.\n\n\"the stats shown outside a fight are now calculated from fewer inputs\" — I think this is the Gear tab's stats. We tested extensively. Could the bug be that the stats list **doesn't include the Ranged/Magic weapon bonuses** because those inputs were dropped? Un-testable without a ranged weapon. But maybe the game has a **starter bow** in the shop; buying one would cost coins and add an item (data change beyond testing? Buying a bow to test Ranged stats is reasonably testing). The shop's Keep one of each toggle off, no item locked. We have 2.5M coins. Could buy a bow and arrows, equip, and check the stats list. But this changes inventory/coins; reversible by selling? The shop may buy back? Risky. And the precondition says \"Do not change data outside what testing requires.\" Buying a ranged weapon to test Ranged stats is arguably required to test the stat list's inputs, but it would alter inventory and coins, which we can't fully revert (coins lost). Hmm, maybe we can sell it back (shop might have sell). But that's more data churn and could break the baseline.\n\nLet me check the Shop quickly to see if ranged weapons are available and whether the stats list would be expected to show Ranged. But buying is unnecessary if we reason.\n\nActually, the key phrase ", "truncated": true}
