is yellow at the far right (x~1000), and the white/grey text \"aids\" ends right before it (x~880). It looks like \"aids\" and \"+10% XP\" are adjacent with no space, but not overlapping. For \"Tiny Templar\": \"A small fish that boosts your +10% XP\" — \"your\" ends at ~895, badge starts ~915. Fine. The row height accommodates two description lines; the badge is vertically centered on the first line. It's a bit tight but acceptable. Not a bug worth reporting.\n\nWait, the element coordinates: description center x=682 with width maybe 700 (from 460 to 900); badge center x=981 width ~130 (915-1045). So no overlap. Good.\n\nNow, the **pet list's last item Bumblebee** is cut off at the bottom? The screenshot showed Bumblebee fully visible with \"+5% XP\". The list scrolls. Fine.\n\nI'm ready to sign off. But let me first ensure the baseline state is correct:\n- No session (Home shows No Active Session). ✓\n- Queue empty — where is the queue shown? Not visible; preconditions said empty and we didn't add. ✓\n- Equipment: Iron Sword + Bronze Boots. ✓ (Gear tab shows Iron Sword, Boots; others None; capes back in inventory.)\n- Combat style Attack. ✓\n- Coins unchanged 2.5M. ✓\n- Items restored. ✓\n\nOne thing: I equipped/unequipped the Agility Cape, which may have toggled its \"equipped\" state; the inventory shows it back. Fine.\n\nI might quickly verify the Inventory shows Agility Cape ×1 and Mercantile Cape ×1 and all items. The last inventory check (before cape test) showed both capes. After unequipping the Agility Cape, it should be back. The Gear tab shows Cape None. Good.\n\nLet me also verify the Profile **Skills** levels didn't change (no XP awarded from abandoned sessions). Home Combat Level 80, Total 720 unchanged. ✓\n\nOkay. But I'm still concerned about the pets tab. Let me make one more attempt to spot a bug there by comparing the **pet count \"0 / 30\"** with the **Armory \"16 / 367\"** and the **Achievements \"12 / 38\"** progress percentages:\n- Pets 0/30 